hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2847","###\n Narrated to us by Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala', he said: Narrated to us by Sufyan, he said: Narrated to us by Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Usama informed me that when the Prophet (ﷺ) set out from Arafat that evening, he let me ride behind him. When we reached the valley (al-Shi'b), he dismounted, relieved himself, and did not perform a full ablution (Ihrāq"
